course: dictionary
lesson: 10215
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. Titanic with a small t means enormous. Titanic with a capital T is a name: the Titanic was a famous ship. «About nine tenths of an iceberg is hidden below the sea, which is why ships keep far away, as the Titanic found out in 1912.» The capital T and the words about the sea and the iceberg show that it names the ship.
explain: «For Titanic in 1997, the filmmakers built a large part of the ship and used models, water tanks and computer effects instead of sinking a real ship.» Here the filmmakers and the film clue you in: Titanic is the name of a film about the ship. Always ask: what does this word point to in this sentence?
explain: When titanic is an adjective, it describes something huge, like «a titanic struggle» or «a titanic effort». Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A huge struggle» still makes sense, so titanic means huge.
fact: Titanic (adjective) means extremely big, strong or important; huge.
fact: The Titanic was a giant British passenger ship that hit an iceberg and sank in the North Atlantic on its first voyage in 1912.
fact: More than 1,500 people died when the Titanic sank.
fact: After the disaster, the rules for safety at sea changed, because there were not enough lifeboats.
fact: In Greek myths, titanic has to do with the Titans, a race of giant gods.
exercise: In «a titanic struggle», what does titanic mean? | *Huge and very hard | Sleepy and calm | Wet and cold | Tiny and quick
exercise: «The Titanic hit an iceberg in 1912.» What was the Titanic? | A small fishing boat | *A giant passenger ship | A shiny stone | A type of cloud
exercise: In «the sinking of the Titanic», what does Titanic name? | A kind of weather | A bird that lives on ice | A feeling of sadness | *A famous ship
test: «The team made a titanic effort to win the race.» What does titanic mean here? | Quiet and gentle | *Huge and very great | Wet and muddy | Small and weak
test: In «The Titanic sailed in 1912», what is Titanic? | A giant god who lives in the sea | *The name of a famous ship | A kind of weather | A feeling of sadness
exam: What do the iceberg sentence and the film sentence show about the word Titanic as a name? | *It can name a ship or a film, so context shows which | It is always a Greek god | It means the same as huge in every sentence | It is always a small word
